# Trivy CVE exceptions for orkyo-community
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # Impact | Reason | Added: YYYY-MM-DD | Review: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Policy: time-bound only. Review date must be within 14 days of added date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available.
#
# 2026-10-09: foundation 1.4.0 moved the Keycloak base to 26.7.5 (community bump ce9a79f).
# A Trivy scan of quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.5 (HIGH+CRITICAL, this day) reports only
# the mssql-jdbc false positive below plus UBI9 pcre2 findings, and the container scan of
# the built orkyo-community-keycloak image on main is green. The Bouncy Castle, netty,
# FreeMarker and four Jackson entries that bridged to this release are gone.
#
# 2026-10-16: foundation 1.6.6 moves the Keycloak base to 26.8.1, which ships mssql-jdbc
# 13.4.0.jre11 (past the fix) on a UBI9 layer with pcre2 10.40-7.el9_8. No active exceptions.
#
# 2026-10-16: upstream rebuilt nginx:1.31-alpine (digest 892bb215, Alpine 3.24.2); a Trivy
# scan at HIGH/CRITICAL with --ignore-unfixed reports 0 findings, so the libexpat, pcre2 and
# libtiff entries are gone with the digest bump in frontend/Dockerfile. The mssql-jdbc entry
# stays: this repo ships foundation 1.6.5's Keycloak 26.7 image, which still carries 13.2.1.
#
# 2026-10-27: upstream rebuilt nginx:1.31-alpine on 2026-10-21 (digest a3554c0d); the libexpat
# and libx11 findings are gone with the digest bump in frontend/Dockerfile. The rebuild still
# predates the Alpine brotli 1.2.1-r0 and curl 8.23.0-r0 packages, hence the two nginx entries.
#
# 2026-11-05: upstream rebuilt nginx:1.31-alpine (digest 785835ea). It still carries the brotli and
# curl packages above and adds three libexpat findings, so the digest bump keeps the two entries and
# adds three. The .NET bases move to 10.0.14 (GHSA-p3jp-9v83-76w9), as orkyo-saas#388 did.

# ── Keycloak base OS layer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2026-09-03: the KC-26.6.x-era entries that stood in this file (jackson-databind,
# micrometer, OpenJDK, libacl, pgjdbc, six netty, a jackson-core GHSA, and the two sqlite
# FTS5 ones) are gone from the image this repo actually ships — the nightly security refresh
# rebuilt the foundation KC base out from under them. Verified against the artifact CI scans,
# ghcr.io/kymr10n/orkyo-community-keycloak:sha-b1290a37, both with CI's flags and with
# --ignore-unfixed OFF: the only findings are the mssql-jdbc false positive above and the
# entry below.
#
# 2026-10-27: foundation's Keycloak base 26.8-orkyo-1.6.10 is built on upstream digest 79c623a.
# Trivy now reports the ca-certificates advisory below on that layer. Upstream digest a78d6b7
# carries the fixed package and foundation adopted it the same day (foundation #287); the next
# foundation bump that ships a rebuilt base drops the entry.

# 2026-10-28: Keycloak 26.8.1, the newest upstream release, ships Guava 33.6.0-jre. Trivy reports
# the deserialization DoS below; Guava 33.7.2 fixes it, and no Keycloak release carries it yet.
#
# 2026-11-13: both entries above passed their review date. The scan of the Keycloak image built on
# the pinned foundation base (26.8-orkyo-1.10.0) no longer reports the ca-certificates advisory, so
# that entry is gone. It still reports Guava 33.6.0-jre, so the Guava entry is renewed; it was first
# added on 2026-10-28.
CVE-2026-102554  # HIGH | guava 33.6.0-jre (lib/main in the Keycloak base 26.8-orkyo-1.10.0): denial of service through unthrottled memory allocation during deserialization, fixed in 33.7.2. Clients reach Keycloak over HTTP with form and JSON bodies only, and its embedded Infinispan cache marshals with ProtoStream, not Java serialization of client input. Drop with the foundation bump that ships a Keycloak base on Guava 33.7.2 or later. | Added: 2026-11-13 | Review: 2026-11-27

# 2026-11-05: Oracle's 2026-10 CPU fixes the OpenJDK font-rendering CVE below. The foundation 1.9.0
# Keycloak base still ships java-21-openjdk-headless 21.0.12; the next foundation release rebuilds it.
CVE-2026-91415  # HIGH | java-21-openjdk-headless 1:21.0.12.1.1-1.2.el9 (foundation 1.9.0 Keycloak base): font rendering flaw, fixed in 1:21.0.13.0.9-1.2.el9. Keycloak renders its login and account pages as HTML and rasterizes no client-supplied fonts in the JVM. Drop with the foundation bump that ships a Keycloak base on OpenJDK 21.0.13 or later. | Added: 2026-11-05 | Review: 2026-11-19

# ── nginx base, waiting for the upstream rebuild ──────────────────────────────

# 2026-11-13: upstream rebuilt nginx:1.31-alpine (digest 713fc2eb, Alpine 3.24.4). The brotli, curl
# and libexpat findings are gone with the digest bump in frontend/Dockerfile, so their entries are
# gone too. The rebuild predates the Alpine libxslt 1.1.43-r4 package, hence the three entries below.
CVE-2026-125350  # HIGH | libxslt 1.1.43-r3: use after free in XML processing, in the nginx:1.31-alpine base (digest 713fc2eb); Alpine fixed it in 1.1.43-r4 but the upstream rebuild predates that package. Only the xslt_filter dynamic module links libxslt; the frontend loads no dynamic module and has no xslt directive. Drop with the next digest bump that carries the fix. | Added: 2026-11-13 | Review: 2026-11-27
CVE-2026-87636  # HIGH | libxslt 1.1.43-r3: type confusion in XML processing, in the nginx:1.31-alpine base (digest 713fc2eb); Alpine fixed it in 1.1.43-r4 but the upstream rebuild predates that package. Only the xslt_filter dynamic module links libxslt; the frontend loads no dynamic module and has no xslt directive. Drop with the next digest bump that carries the fix. | Added: 2026-11-13 | Review: 2026-11-27
CVE-2026-9947  # HIGH | libxslt 1.1.43-r3: use after free in XML processing, in the nginx:1.31-alpine base (digest 713fc2eb); Alpine fixed it in 1.1.43-r4 but the upstream rebuild predates that package. Only the xslt_filter dynamic module links libxslt; the frontend loads no dynamic module and has no xslt directive. Drop with the next digest bump that carries the fix. | Added: 2026-11-13 | Review: 2026-11-27
